# Aston Martin DB4 Series I fixed-head coupe, 1958-1963.
#
# The DB4, the Touring Superleggera-bodied GT that replaced the DB Mk III, on
# sale from 1958 to 1963. The Series I fixed-head coupe is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DB4 (The Motor road test, 1960,
# cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.4958 x 1.6764 x 1.3335 m, wheelbase 2.4892 m, converted from the
# pack's 177 x 66 x 52.5 in and 98 in figures. The model is 4.4845 m long
# (11.3 mm short of the published figure) on the 2.4892 m wheelbase (55.4 per
# cent), 1.6764 m wide and 1.3335 m high.
#
# Shape reference: images 1 and 3 are the same red Series I car and image 2 is a
# different 1959 Series I of the same body, as the pack states. The model has
# the **exposed headlamps** of the DB4, not the DB5's fairings, the wide Aston
# grille, the rounded fastback tail with the early small lamps, chrome wire
# wheels and a small bumper at each end.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found (grade d); cars of this era
# were finished to order, so the objects carry plain names: British Racing
# Green, silver, black and red. Weights green 3, silver 3, black 2, red 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 225 km/h, the car's quoted maximum. Comfort 58/267, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 58: a light, low GT of 1958. Classes 3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1958 intro, retires staggered 1973-1976 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-db4.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-db4.dae (251 objects). References:
# citycars/references/aston-db4/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the comparisons use approximate camera angles and the
# side elevation was rendered for coherence rather than matched to a true side
# photograph. Glazing stands about 15 mm clear of its supporting surfaces. At
# 128 px the rounded Touring body with its exposed headlamps reads as a DB4.

obj=citycar
name=AstonDB4(BritishRacingGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1958
intro_month=1
retire_year=1976
retire_month=6
speed=225
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=58
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=267

